The P() operation (also known as `wait()` or `acquire()`) is atomic and typically implemented as:
```
P(S):
  S.value--;
  if (S.value < 0) {
    add this process to S.queue;
    block this process;
  }
```
If $S.value$ becomes negative, it implies that the requested resource is unavailable, and the calling process must wait.

The V() operation (also known as `signal()` or `release()`) is atomic and typically implemented as:
```
V(S):
  S.value++;
  if (S.value <= 0) {
    remove a process P from S.queue;
    wakeup process P;
  }
```
If $S.value$ is still non-positive after incrementing, it means there were processes waiting, and one should be unblocked.
